    "solution_text": "The radius is $1$, so Pythagoras' theorem gives $u^2+v^2=1$. Substituting the coordinates gives\n$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2\\alpha+\\sin^2\\alpha&=1.\\end{align*}$\nThe circle equation holds in every quadrant, so the identity holds for every real $\\alpha$.",
