  {
    "question_text": "Starting with $\\cos^2\\beta+\\sin^2\\beta=1$, derive the identities involving (a) tangent and secant and (b) cotangent and cosecant. State the condition for each division.",
    "solution_text": "(a) Divide every term by $\\cos^2\\beta$, where $\\cos\\beta\\ne0$.\n$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\cos^2\\beta}{\\cos^2\\beta}+\\frac{\\sin^2\\beta}{\\cos^2\\beta}&=\\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\beta}\\\\1+\\tan^2\\beta&=\\sec^2\\beta.\\end{align*}$\n(b) Divide every term by $\\sin^2\\beta$, where $\\sin\\beta\\ne0$.\n$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\cos^2\\beta}{\\sin^2\\beta}+\\frac{\\sin^2\\beta}{\\sin^2\\beta}&=\\frac{1}{\\sin^2\\beta}\\\\\\cot^2\\beta+1&=\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\beta.\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
