  {
    "question_text": "Simplify using the Pythagorean identities: (a) $1-\\sin^2\\gamma$, (b) $\\tan^2\\gamma-\\sec^2\\gamma$, (c) $1+\\cot^2\\gamma$, (d) $\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\gamma-1$.",
    "solution_text": "(a)\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}1-\\sin^2\\gamma\\\\&=\\cos^2\\gamma.\\end{align*}$\n(b)\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\tan^2\\gamma-\\sec^2\\gamma\\\\&=\\tan^2\\gamma-(1+\\tan^2\\gamma)\\\\&=-1.\\end{align*}$\n(c)\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}1+\\cot^2\\gamma\\\\&=\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\gamma.\\end{align*}$\n(d)\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\gamma-1\\\\&=(1+\\cot^2\\gamma)-1\\\\&=\\cot^2\\gamma.\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
