  {
    "question_text": "Simplify: (a) $7\\cot^2\\alpha+7$, (b) $6\\sin^2\\alpha-6\\sin^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\alpha$, (c) $4-\\tan^2\\alpha+\\sec^2\\alpha$.",
    "solution_text": "(a) Factor out $7$.\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}7\\cot^2\\alpha+7\\\\&=7(\\cot^2\\alpha+1)\\\\&=7\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\alpha.\\end{align*}$\n(b) Factor out $6\\sin^2\\alpha$.\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}6\\sin^2\\alpha-6\\sin^2\\alpha\\cos^2\\alpha\\\\&=6\\sin^2\\alpha(1-\\cos^2\\alpha)\\\\&=6\\sin^2\\alpha\\sin^2\\alpha\\\\&=6\\sin^4\\alpha.\\end{align*}$\n(c)\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}4-\\tan^2\\alpha+\\sec^2\\alpha\\\\&=4-\\tan^2\\alpha+(1+\\tan^2\\alpha)\\\\&=5.\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
      "mode": "continuation"
    }
  },
  {
    "question_text": "Simplify: (a) $\\cot^2\\beta-\\dfrac{1}{\\sin^2\\beta}$, (b) $\\dfrac{5\\sec^2\\beta-5}{\\sec^2\\beta}$. Assume $\\sin\\beta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\beta\\ne0$.",
    "solution_text": "(a) Rewrite the reciprocal using cosecant.\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\cot^2\\beta-\\frac{1}{\\sin^2\\beta}\\\\&=\\cot^2\\beta-\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\beta\\\\&=\\cot^2\\beta-(1+\\cot^2\\beta)\\\\&=-1.\\end{align*}$\n(b) Use the secant identity, then write the ratios in sine and cosine.\n$\\begin{align*}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\frac{5\\sec^2\\beta-5}{\\sec^2\\beta}\\\\&=\\frac{5(\\sec^2\\beta-1)}{\\sec^2\\beta}\\\\&=\\frac{5\\tan^2\\beta}{\\sec^2\\beta}\\\\&=\\frac{5\\left(\\frac{\\sin^2\\beta}{\\cos^2\\beta}\\right)}{\\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\beta}}\\\\&=5\\sin^2\\beta.\\end{align*}$",
    "equationAlignment": {
